Sandip Mukherjee was born in West Bengal, India, in 1984. He received his B.Sc. in chemistry in 2005 from the University of Calcutta and M.Sc. in chemistry in 2007 from IIT- Madras. Since 2007, he has been working with Prof. P. S. Mukherjee in the Indian Institute of Science for Ph.D. His principal research interest concerns various aspects of molecular magnetism and application of density functional theory in molecular magnetism.
Partha Sarathi Mukherjee received his Ph.D. in 2002 working with Prof. N. Ray Chaudhuri at Indian Association for the Cultivation of Science, and his postdoctoral from University of Utah with Prof. Peter J. Stang. In 2004, he moved to University of Goettingen to work with Prof. Herbert W. Roesky as a Humboldt fellow. He has been at the Indian Institute of Science, Bangalore, since July 2005, where he is currently an Associate Professor. His current research interests are in the areas of self-assembly of functional molecular architectures and magnetic polyclusters. He is the recipient of a young scientist medal of the Indian National Science Academy, Associateship of the Indian Academy of Sciences, Young Affiliate Fellowship of the Third World Academy of Sciences (Trieste), Swarnajayanti Fellowship of Govt. of India, SCOPUS young scientist award by Elsevier, and Microsoft Research outstanding young faculty award. Dr. Mukherjee has published 103 original papers in peer-reviewed journals.
